    live_deploy: close DeployedTreeRemoteUnit by reading its own typed oneshot unit file
    
    The tree-remote convergence oneshot was NotYetModeled ("ExecStart not exported by its module"). Its module
    (repository_convergence_placement) does model it — as a typed ConvergenceOneshot whose ExecStart/WorkingDirectory
    the host text is serialized from. Manager's item-1 rule: "closes the same way once its module exports its unit
    file." So:
    
    - repository_convergence_placement: factor convergence_oneshot_service_unit_file(slice, oneshot) -> SystemdUnitFile
      out of convergence_oneshot_text_in (pure extract; the host text is now serialize(that file)). ONE authority for
      what a oneshot runs.
    - emit: live_deploy_tree_remote_unit_file_for_closure(spec) builds that file, at the ADMITTED convergence slice,
      from the same tree_remote_convergence_oneshot the deploy emits — Absent only when the slice is refused.
    - adapter: DeployedTreeRemoteUnit => unit_file_read_set(<the accessor>) — the SAME argv[0]/WorkingDirectory readers
      the doors/broker/serve use. No second parser (item-1 rule).
    
    Control the_tree_remote_read_set_matches_the_emitted_host_text compares the CLOSURE read against the SERIALIZED
    host text (convergence_oneshot_unit_text), not against the shared helper: it goes red if the readers drift from
    what the serialization emits. srv1 admits the convergence slice (unit is Declared); a refused slice is not
    silently green. Regressions a_fresh_host / roster / every_enabled_step PASS on base-matched seed sha256 900599bd...
    
    Node: deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure (node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59).

